@* Material 3 overflow menu (md-menu, anchored off an md-icon-button "more actions" trigger) consolidating
   the less-frequently-used per-printer actions - Push Bag Tag Templates, Calibrate Media, Factory
   Reset - so PrinterDashboard.razor's button row doesn't keep growing every time a new maintenance
   action is added (it'd reached ~7 buttons across the two pages this replaced before this).
   Configure/Reconfigure Printer and the Web Interface toggle stay directly visible outside this menu -
   see WebInterfaceTogglePanel's own doc comment for why the toggle specifically isn't here. "Abandon
   this printer" is PrinterDashboard's own standalone "Disconnect Printer" button, not a menu item
   here - this menu used to also carry a Pairing.razor-only "Start Over" item for that before the
   dashboard consolidation gave every arrival path the same button instead. Recheck Configuration was
   also removed - PrinterDashboard's own "About Printer" link already re-reads and shows the printer's
   current status, making a separate recheck action here redundant.

   FactoryResetPanel/BagTagTemplatesPanel/CalibrateMediaButton no longer render their own trigger
   buttons - the host page still renders those three components directly (elsewhere in its markup, so
   their own confirm dialogs/progress/results still show up in the normal page flow, not swallowed by
   this menu closing), and passes @ref-captured references here so this menu's items can call each
   one's public Request*Async() trigger method.

   _open sync: md-menu closes itself on item click/outside click/Escape via real browser JS this app
   never executes in tests, and Blazor's short "@onclosed" syntax only binds well-known DOM events -
   a genuinely custom event like md-menu's "closed" needs an explicit JS interop event registration to
   bind at all (confirmed: it silently no-ops otherwise), which felt like too much machinery to add
   for this. So instead, every ITEM click below also explicitly sets _open = false itself (covering the
   overwhelmingly common "selected an action" case exactly) - only the narrower "dismissed via outside
   click/Escape without selecting anything" path can leave _open stale, in which case the very next
   anchor tap is a no-op (toggles an already-effectively-closed menu) and the tap after that reopens it
   correctly. Accepted as a minor, rare-path rough edge rather than adding a JS interop module to a
   project that otherwise has none beyond the vendored Material Web bundle. *@
<span class="printer-actions-menu-anchor">
    <md-icon-button id="@AnchorId" data-testid="printer-actions-menu-button" aria-label="More actions" @onclick="() => _open = !_open">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path fill="currentColor" d="M12 8c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2s-.9-2-2-2-2 .9-2 2 .9 2 2 2zm0 2c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2s.9 2 2 2 2-.9 2-2-.9-2-2-2zm0 6c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2s.9 2 2 2 2-.9 2-2-.9-2-2-2z" />
        </svg>
    </md-icon-button>
    @* positioning="fixed" (not the default "absolute") - the anchor lives inside
       MainLayout's .function-section, which scrolls its own overflow; an "absolute"-positioned
       popup is clipped at that container's boundary once it has enough items to run past the
       visible viewport, making the lower items unreachable with no way to scroll to them. "fixed"
       positions relative to the viewport instead, escaping that clipping entirely. *@
    <md-menu anchor="@AnchorId" open="@(_open)" positioning="fixed" data-testid="printer-actions-menu">
        <md-menu-item data-testid="menu-item-push-bag-tag-templates" @onclick="() => Select(OnPushBagTagTemplates)">
            <div slot="headline">Push Bag Tag Templates</div>
        </md-menu-item>
        <md-menu-item data-testid="menu-item-calibrate-media" @onclick="() => Select(OnCalibrateMedia)">
            <div slot="headline">Calibrate Media</div>
        </md-menu-item>
        <md-menu-item data-testid="menu-item-factory-reset" @onclick="() => Select(OnFactoryReset)">
            <div slot="headline">Factory Reset</div>
        </md-menu-item>
    </md-menu>
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The anchor md-icon-button's element id, referenced by md-menu's own "anchor" attribute -
    /// each host page passes its own literal id (never two of these menus render at once, so a
    /// fixed string per page is fine).
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string AnchorId { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public EventCallback OnPushBagTagTemplates { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public EventCallback OnCalibrateMedia { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public EventCallback OnFactoryReset { get; set; }

    private bool _open;

    private Task Select(EventCallback callback)
    {
        _open = false;
        return callback.InvokeAsync();
    }
}
